  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Mechanism
    
    A Nightshelf perceptual-denial technique. Veil∴numb does not render the practitioner invisible; it induces a wrongness in observers' perception that causes attention to slide past the user as though they occupy a gap in the world's notice. The effect manifests as a gradual cooling of the surrounding air and a flattening of light across the practitioner's form — not darkness but absence of shadow.
    
    The technique requires sustained contact with captured fire held beneath the skin. The opposition of heat against the body's cold generates a pocket of perceptual distortion rooted in fire-magic's transformative properties. It derives from **Slide Prism**, a Nightshelf refraction discipline, but trades that technique's elegance for what can only be described as brutality of application.
    
    ## Origin and Practitioners
    
    Developed at **The Drowned Ledge** by the **Collective☽ Of Led∴merch**, a merchant guild specializing in covert fire-core transport, during **the Frozen Peace**. Notable practitioners include **Depth-Purveyor ☽'Cilocum**, a merchant-mystic of considerable and reportedly uncontrollable power; **☽'Iarlocias the Silent**, a mystic and outlaw who broke with The Communion; and operatives of **The Cell (owl-sworn)**. The technique's spread to **☽'ofund' Guild** and — remarkably — **Qingqe'frostlings**, an Aurora-aligned governing council, suggests proliferation well beyond its Nightshelf origins.
    
    ## Cost
    
    Extended use burns sensation from the extremities inward. Nightshelf oral tradition teaches three stages: loss of cold, loss of pain, loss of awareness of others. The teaching formula — *what you cannot feel, you cannot hold* — is unusually direct for Nightshelf pedagogy. Users report perceiving their own heartbeat as distant, belonging to another body.
    
    ## Historical Significance
    
    Veil∴numb appears as a thread through **The Mbra∴silentiu**, the **Collapse (ice-cracked)**, and the **Breach (ice-screamed)** — moments when negotiated peace fractured and unseen agents moved through chambers unchallenged. The technique did not cause these crises. It made them possible.
